1794129561.619630 {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"agent_message","text":"Stopped at the requested lane-agent handoff. Both roots are claimed and their worktrees and briefs are ready:\n\n- **core — FEAT-001:** [brief](/runs/multi-module/repo.todo/FEAT-001.brief.md), claim commit `d4b06a7`.\n- **text — FEAT-002:** [brief](/runs/multi-module/repo.todo/FEAT-002.brief.md), claim commit `63fd207`.\n\nThe shared regression baseline, `mvn -B test`, passed with **2 tests**, no failures and no skips. Neither lane is blocked; both roots remain open. No lane implementation or merge to base has occurred. The main checkout is on `main`.\n\nThe next workable roots are FEAT-001 in `core` and FEAT-002 in `text`. After the lane agents return, a fresh coordinator should run steps 4 and 5. Clear context for that session.\n\nAmbiguities and conflicts encountered:\n\n- The core says, **“At most one `[/]` task”**, while lanes require each completed root to be left **“`[/]` with `next: drain`”**. I interpreted the invariant as applying within each separate worktree; the coordinator will reconcile roots sequentially.\n- Lane step 3 says each agent **“gets only”** the listed information and rules, while the user also supplied trial-wide restrictions. I included those restrictions in each brief so the agents can follow the user’s instructions.\n- Lane step 1 says to run steps 1–3 **“for the first workable node of every lane”**. Both nodes use the same regression command on the same unchanged base, so I used one successful run as the baseline for both."}}
